Modifications made in this fork, as required by section 4(b) of the License:

- src-tauri/src/imap/client.rs — parenthesised multi-item FETCH data lists so
  strict servers return message bodies.
- src-tauri/src/db_tx.rs (added), src-tauri/src/lib.rs,
  src/services/db/connection.ts — transactions run on a dedicated SQLite
  connection instead of the plugin's connection pool.
- src/services/calendar/davFetch.ts (added),
  src/services/calendar/autoDiscovery.ts,
  src/services/calendar/caldavProvider.ts — CalDAV requests go through the Rust
  HTTP client, and discovery also probes the configured mail server host.
- src/services/db/accounts.ts, src/components/accounts/AddCalDavAccount.tsx —
  CalDAV settings attach to an existing account for the same address.
- src/services/calendar/recurrence.ts (added),
  src/services/calendar/timezone.ts (added),
  src/services/calendar/occurrences.ts (added),
  src/services/calendar/icalHelper.ts, src/services/calendar/types.ts,
  src/services/db/calendarEvents.ts, src/services/db/migrations.ts,
  src/components/calendar/ — recurring CalDAV events are expanded into their
  individual instances on the client. A CalDAV server returns the series master
  rather than expanded instances, so a recurring event previously appeared only
  once. Recurrence is evaluated in the time zone of the series' DTSTART, and the
  iCalendar parser was made component-aware so a VTIMEZONE's own rules are no
  longer read as the event's.
- src/services/calendar/icalEdit.ts (added),
  src/services/calendar/caldavProvider.ts,
  src/components/calendar/EventDetailModal.tsx — edits patch the stored
  calendar object instead of regenerating the VEVENT, which previously
  discarded the recurrence rule, time zone, alarms and per-instance overrides.
  Single occurrences can be changed or removed separately from their series.
- src/services/calendar/errors.ts (added),
  src/services/calendar/caldavProvider.ts, src/services/calendar/icalEdit.ts,
  src/services/calendar/recurrence.ts, src/services/calendar/types.ts,
  src/services/calendar/googleCalendarProvider.ts,
  src/components/calendar/EventDetailModal.tsx — corrections to the CalDAV
  write paths. If-Match is now taken from the calendar object's etag rather
  than passed as a headers parameter, which tsdav merges over the
  authorization header so every PUT and DELETE was refused with 401. A refused
  write raises an error instead of being reported as saved, with 412 shown as
  a conflict. Splitting a series stores the remainder before bounding the
  original and takes it back if that fails, and rebases the rule's COUNT so
  the two halves add up to the original series. UNTIL is written with the
  value type DTSTART uses, and cutting a series before its first instance
  deletes the object instead of leaving a series that has no instances.
- src/services/calendar/recurrenceForm.ts (added),
  src/components/calendar/RecurrenceField.tsx (added),
  src/services/calendar/icalHelper.ts, src/services/calendar/icalEdit.ts,
  src/services/calendar/recurrence.ts, src/services/calendar/timezone.ts,
  src/services/calendar/types.ts, src/services/calendar/caldavProvider.ts,
  src/services/calendar/googleCalendarProvider.ts,
  src/components/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx,
  src/components/calendar/EventCreateModal.tsx,
  src/components/calendar/EventDetailModal.tsx — repetition can be set up and
  changed in the dialogs rather than only read. A generated VEVENT now carries
  an RRULE, and an existing rule can be replaced or removed on the series
  master; UNTIL is written with the value type the series' DTSTART uses. A rule
  the control cannot state — an ordinal weekday, a BYSETPOS — is shown but left
  untouched instead of being silently downgraded, and a control nobody touched
  sends nothing at all, so editing a title never rewrites the repetition.
  Changing the rule drops the exceptions and per-instance overrides the old one
  anchored, which the expander would otherwise render as occurrences the series
  no longer has.
- src/components/email/EmailRenderer.tsx, public/emailFrame.js (added) — the
  email body frame reports link clicks and its height over postMessage instead
  of relying on a listener the app attaches to the frame document, which WebKit
  never invokes on a sandboxed frame. The frame now runs on an opaque origin.
- Application identity renamed from Velo (com.velomail.app) to Maish
  (xyz.hochreiner.maish), including packaging metadata, the encryption key file
  name and the update endpoint.
- Upstream-specific material removed: the marketing site, release and packaging
  workflows, contribution and security policies, Velo's changelog, and Velo's
  logo and application icons, which are trademarks and not covered by the
  licence. Icons and logo are original to Maish.

"Velo" is the name of the upstream project and is used here only to identify the
work this fork derives from.
